nty"],["ARC or PLC in Columbus County","/arc-plc/north-carolina/columbus-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 11 grids September to October came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them, more than any other pair. In 2026 so far, March to April sat at 27% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid on the page had its driest year in 2007, and grid 17008 got down to 56% that year.</p>"}
